 },
 "why": "The face between two nodes of a copper layer is built from the copper fill of the cells the face runs through instead of the harmonic mean of the nodal half-copper sheets: the first copper link is the whole copper sheet and the copper edge is not blurred over a cell, so boards with a copper edge inside the board read hotter (closer to the independent 3D solver and the finite-element limit); uniform and hatched copper, outline boards without a copper edge, imported layers and metal-block boards do not move."
